{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (PATIENT): Good morning, doctor. I am very sorry we are late. The auto was stuck near the flyover for almost twenty minutes.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Good morning. Please, don't trouble yourself about that. Sit, both of you. Has the morning been all right otherwise?",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (PATIENT): Yes, thank you, doctor. It was only the traffic. My daughter wished to accompany me.",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I insisted, actually. My nani, her mother, had the gallbladder removed last year in Coimbatore, and amma has been scared by everyone's stories since then.",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (DOCTOR): I can imagine. Umm, stories like that stay in the mind. What have you yourself been feeling, though?",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (PATIENT): Doctor, I am having pain on the right side of my upper stomach. It comes after I eat oily food.",
  "[SEG0007] person_4 (NURSE): Sorry to come in, doctor. I checked madam's vitals outside only. Blood pressure is 132 over 84, pulse is 78, temperature is 36.8, oxygen saturation is 98 percent.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (DOCTOR): Thank you, sister. This pain, when did it begin?",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (PATIENT): It started two months ago, doctor. I thought it was only gas.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (DOCTOR): When it is there, what is it like, and where do you feel it?",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (PATIENT): The pain itself sits just under the right ribs. For two months it has been quite severe, and I have to stop my class and sit. It comes after oily food, lasts two or three hours, and the antacid brings it down only a little.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She leaves her tea untouched, doctor. She just lies down and holds that side.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (DOCTOR): Mm. Is it every meal, or certain foods?",
  "[SEG0014] person_1 (PATIENT): Fatty food mainly, doctor. Ghee, poori, those fried snacks. Last Sunday it was mutton biryani at my cousin's, and she always cooks for a crowd.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (DOCTOR): And, err, have you vomited with these pains?",
  "[SEG0016] person_1 (PATIENT): No, doctor. I have not vomited.",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any fever, even a small one?",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (PATIENT): No doctor. No fever.",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any yellowing of the eyes or the skin?",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (PATIENT): No, doctor. There is no yellow colour.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (DOCTOR): How about the stool? Has the colour become pale, or very dark?",
  "[SEG0022] person_1 (PATIENT): The pain comes about one hour after I finish eating, doctor. Sometimes a little later if I eat slowly.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. One hour, that is worth knowing. Err, I had asked about the stool colour as well. Has that changed?",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (PATIENT): Forgive me, doctor, I went to the other point. No, the colour has not changed. It is not pale.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (DOCTOR): Quite all right. Does the pain spread to the shoulder or the back?",
  "[SEG0026] person_1 (PATIENT): To the right shoulder blade, sometimes. Not the back.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (DOCTOR): Umm. Any burning in the chest between these attacks?",
  "[SEG0028] person_1 (PATIENT): A little, doctor, now and then. It is mild. The pain is my real trouble.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (DOCTOR): What have you taken for it?",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (PATIENT): I swallow two Gelucil tablets by mouth when the pain starts. It helps a little, not completely.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (DOCTOR): How many times would that be?",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (PATIENT): On the days I have eaten oily food, two times or three times. I am not on any other medicine, doctor.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (DOCTOR): That is perfectly fine for now. Have you had any operation in the past?",
  "[SEG0034] person_1 (PATIENT): Only a caesarean, when my daughter was born. Twenty two years ago. Nothing since.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (DOCTOR): And in the family, other than your mother, anyone with gallbladder trouble?",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (PATIENT): No, doctor. Only my mother. They told her there were stones, and then they did the surgery.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (DOCTOR): Let me ask about passing urine. Any burning, or going too frequently?",
  "[SEG0038] person_1 (PATIENT): No doctor. Urine is normal.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any cough or shortness of breath, anything with the chest?",
  "[SEG0040] person_1 (PATIENT): No, doctor. The chest is clear. I teach at the corporation primary school, and I walk there every day.",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (DOCTOR): Appetite, or your weight, any change?",
  "[SEG0042] person_1 (PATIENT): Appetite is a bit less when the pain is there. My weight is the same. Last month the scale here showed fifty eight kilograms.",
  "[SEG0043] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She does eat, doctor. Only smaller amounts on those days.",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (DOCTOR): You said you have not vomited. Uh, is there nausea, that sick feeling, even so?",
  "[SEG0045] person_1 (PATIENT): Well, actually, uh, doctor, please let me correct that. I am sorry. After the biryani that evening I did vomit, once only. The food came up, and then the pain eased a little.",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (DOCTOR): I am glad you said so. Just that single episode?",
  "[SEG0047] person_1 (PATIENT): Yes, doctor. Only once. Not again.",
  "[SEG0048] person_2 (DOCTOR): Let me feel the tummy. It is soft. There is definite tenderness under the right ribs. No guarding, and I cannot feel a lump.",
  "[SEG0049] person_2 (DOCTOR): Putting it together, the pain after oily meals and this tenderness, this is most likely biliary colic, pain from the gallbladder, possibly from stones. That is my working view. I would not call it certain yet.",
  "[SEG0050] person_2 (DOCTOR): I am arranging blood tests today, a liver function test and a full blood count, and an ultrasound of the abdomen.",
  "[SEG0051] person_4 (NURSE): I will take her across for the blood draw, doctor, and I will book the ultrasound for tomorrow morning at imaging.",
  "[SEG0052] person_2 (DOCTOR): Good. Please continue two Gelucil tablets when the pain comes, avoid oily and fried food, and if the pain becomes constant, or the vomiting repeats, or the eyes turn yellow, go to casualty the same day. Come back in one week with the reports.",
  "[SEG0053] person_1 (PATIENT): Yes, doctor. I will do exactly that. Thank you very much.",
  "[SEG0054] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): We will come with the reports. Thank you, doctor."
 ],
